      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 463,
      "output": "At its most fundamental level, **water** is a chemical compound and one of the most abundant and essential substances on Earth. \n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, looking at it through different lenses:\n\n### 1. The Chemical View\n* **Formula ($H_2O$):** Each molecule of water is made up of **two hydrogen atoms** bonded to **one oxygen atom**. \n* **The \"Universal Solvent\":** Because of its chemical structure, water is slightly charged (polar). This makes it exceptionally good at dissolving other substances, which is why it can easily carry minerals, nutrients, and chemicals through our bodies and the environment.\n* **Three States:** Water is unique because it is the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three physical states:\n  * **Liquid** (the water we drink, rivers, oceans)\n  * **Solid** (ice, snow, glaciers)\n  * **Gas** (water vapor, steam, humidity)\n\n### 2. The Ecological View (Earth’s Lifeblood)\n* **Coverage:** About **71% of the Earth's surface** is covered by water, mostly in the oceans (which hold about 96.5% of all Earth's water).\n* **The Water Cycle:** Water is constantly recycling itself through evaporation, condensation, and precipitation (rain and snow). The water you drink today is the exact same water that dinosaurs drank millions of years ago.\n* **Climate Regulator:** Oceans and water vapor absorb and distribute heat around the globe, regulating the Earth's weather and climate.\n\n### 3. The Biological View (The Essence of Life)\n* **Biology:** Life as we know it cannot exist without water. It provides the medium in which all the metabolic and cellular processes of life take place.\n* **Human Body:** The human body is made up of about **60% water**. It relies on water to regulate temperature, lubricate joints, flush out waste, and transport nutrients through the blood.\n\n### Summary\nIn short, water is a simple molecule that performs a monumental job. It is the cradle of life, a geological shaper of planets, and a precious resource that connects all living things."
